# login.defs - shadow password suite configuration.
#
# Read by anything that needs default UID/GID ranges or password aging
# policy without hardcoding them (useradd/adduser, and desktop login
# managers like sddm filtering system accounts off the user list).

UID_MIN                  1000
UID_MAX                 60000
SYS_UID_MIN                 1
SYS_UID_MAX                999

GID_MIN                  1000
GID_MAX                 60000
SYS_GID_MIN                  1
SYS_GID_MAX                999

PASS_MAX_DAYS            99999
PASS_MIN_DAYS                0
PASS_WARN_AGE                7

# toybox's chpasswd/login only understand the traditional crypt(3) DES/
# MD5/SHA schemes, not yescrypt - YESCRYPT here silently produced a
# password chpasswd itself couldn't verify ("login: bad salt" for every
# login attempt, root effectively locked out). Confirmed by testing
# both directly: `chpasswd` with no -c flag (reads this file) failed;
# `chpasswd -c SHA512` worked and produced a real, verifiable $6$ hash.
ENCRYPT_METHOD          SHA512
